#
# What one care item costs over a month (poultice_rules.h PR4), in Sutra,
# in integer minor units: a unit's price in 9(9), the units used a day in
# 9(3) and the month's days in 9(2) (solstice.month_days), the cost
# price * perday * days in 9(15). A negative value, or one with more
# digits, does not fit its picture: refused, never wrapped, where cost.tb
# answers it: held.
record care-cost
  price: 9(9)
  perday: 9(3)
  days: 9(2)
  cost: 9(15)
procedure
  compute cost = price * perday * days
  answer cost
